§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And God gave Solomon wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that is on the sea shore.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnAnd Solomon's wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east country, and all the wisdom of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšFor he was wiser than all men; than Ethan the Ezrahite, and Heman, and Chalcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol: and his fame was in all nations round about.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd he spake three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿And he spake of trees, from the cedar tree that is in Lebanon even unto the hyssop that springeth out of the wall: he spake also of beasts, and of fowl, and of creeping things, and of fishes.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd there came of all people to hear the wisdom of Solomon, from all kings of the earth, which had heard of his wisdom.¦layout ªlast_verse"